{
  "title": "Taweez against Fever",
  "data": "(1) It is recommended to say this supplicatory amulet, which the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) taught to Imam Ali (a.s.) against fever:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ ارْحَمْ جِلْدِىَ الرَّقِيْقَ وَعَظْمِىَ الدَّقِيْقَ وَاَعُوْذُ بِكَ مِنْ فَوْرَةِ الْحَرِيْقِ\nALLAAHUMMAR HAM JILDIYAR RAQEEQA WA A'ZMIYAD DAQEEQA WA A'OODHU BIKA MIN FAWRATIL HAREEQ\nO Allah, have mercy on my thin skin and my frail bones, and I seek refuge in You from the outburst of burning heat.\nيَاۤ اُمَّ مِلْدَمٍ اِنْ كُنْتِ اٰمَنْتِ بِاللّٰهِ فَلَا تَاْكُلِى اللَّحْمَ وَلَا تَشْرَبِى الدَّمَ\nYAA UMMA MILDAMIN IN KUNTI AAMANTI BILLAAHI FALAA TA'KULIL LAHMA WA LAA TASHRABID DAM\nO Umm Mildam (fever)! If you believe in Allah, then do not eat the flesh, do not drink the blood,\nوَلَا تَفُوْرِىْ مِنَ الْفَمِ وَانْتَقِلِىْ اِلٰى مَنْ يَّزْعَمُ اَنَّ مَعَ اللّٰهِ اِلٰهًا اٰخَرَ\nWA LAA TAFOOREE MINAL FAMI WANTAQILEE ILAA MAN YAZ'AMU ANNA MA'ALLAAHI ILAAHAN AAKHAR\nand do not boil up from the mouth; move away to him who claims that there is another god with Allah,\nفَاِنِّىْ اَشْهَدُ اَنْ لَّاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ وَحْدَهٗ لَا شَرِيْكَ لَهٗ وَاَشْهَدُ اَنَّ مُحَمَّدًا عَبْدُهٗ وَرَسُوْلُهٗ\nFA-INNEE ASH-HADU AL LAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAHU WAHDAHOO LAA SHAREEKA LAHOO WA ASH-HADU ANNA MUHAMMADAN A'BDUHOO WA RASOOLUH\nfor I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, One, having no partner, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger.\n(2) A feverish person is recommended to say, mornings and evenings, the supplicatory prayer known as [Dua Noor](E33), which Lady Fatimah al-Zahra (s.a.) taught to Salman.\n(3) The Holy Imams (a.s.) are reported to have treated themselves against fever with cold water. They used to wet two garments, putting one on and leaving the other in water; when the one they wore dried out, they would put on the other, wet one.\n(4) As written by Imam al-Reza (a.s.), a feverish person may write the following inscriptions on three sheets of paper. On the first sheet:\nبِسْمِ اللّٰهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ لَا تَخَفْ اِنَّكَ اَنْتَ الْاَعْلٰى\nBISMILLAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEMI LAA TAKHAF INNAKA ANTAL A'LAA\nIn the Name of Allah, the Beneficent, the Merciful. Fear not, surely you shall be the uppermost. (20:68)\nOn the second sheet:\nبِسْمِ اللّٰهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ لَا تَخَفْ نَجَوْتَ مِنَ الْقَوْمِ الظَّالِمِيْنَ\nBISMILLAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEMI LAA TAKHAF NAJAWTA MINAL QAWMIZ ZAALIMEEN\nIn the Name of Allah, the Beneficent, the Merciful. Fear not, you are secure from the unjust people. (28:25)\nOn the third sheet:\nبِسْمِ اللّٰهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ اَلَا لَهُ الْخَلْقُ وَالْاَمْرُ تَبَارَكَ اللّٰهُ رَبُّ الْعَالَمِيْنَ\nBISMILLAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEMI ALAA LAHUL KHALQU WAL AMRU TABAARAKALLAAHU RABBUL A'ALAMEEN\nIn the Name of Allah, the Beneficent, the Merciful. Surely His is the creation and the command; blessed is Allah, the Lord of the worlds. (7:54)\nOver each of these sheets, [Surah al-Tawhid](A116) may be recited three times. The feverish person may then swallow the sheets over three days, one each day. If this is done, the fever will be healed, Allah willing.\n(5) The feverish person may undo the buttons of his shirt, put his head inside it towards his chest, say the adhan and the iqamah, and recite [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) seven times. If this is done, the fever will be healed, Allah willing.\n(6) The Holy Imams (a.s.) are reported to have instructed that the following supplicatory prayer should be written on a parchment and hung on the feverish person:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّىْ اَسْئَلُكَ بِعِزَّتِكَ وَقُدْرَتِكَ وَسُلْطَانِكَ وَمَاۤ اَحَاطَ بِهٖ عِلْمُكَ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS'ALUKA BI-I'ZZATIKA WA QUDRATIKA WA SULTAANIKA WA MAA AHAATA BIHEE I'LMUK\nO Allah, I ask You by Your might, Your power, Your authority, and all that Your knowledge encompasses,\nاَنْ تُصَلِّىَ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَّاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ وَّاَنْ لَّا تُسَلِّطَ عَلٰى فُلَانِ بْنِ فُلَانٍ شَيْئًا مِّمَّا خَلَقْتَ بِسُوْۤءٍ\nAN TUSALLIYA A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMADIN WA AL LAA TUSALLITA A'LAA FULAANIBNI FULAANIN SHAY'AM MIMMAA KHALAQTA BISOO'\nto bless Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad, and not to give anything You have created power to harm so-and-so, the son of so-and-so;\nوَارْحَمْ جِلْدَهُ الرَّقِيْقَ وَعَظْمَهُ الدَّقِيْقَ مِنْ فَوْرَةِ الْحَرِيْقِ\nWARHAM JILDAHUR RAQEEQA WA A'ZMAHUD DAQEEQA MIN FAWRATIL HAREEQ\nand have mercy on his thin skin and his frail bones against the outburst of burning heat.\nاُخْرُجِىْ يَاۤ اُمَّ مِلْدَمٍ يَّا اٰكِلَةَ اللَّحْمِ وَشَارِبَةَ الدَّمِ حَرُّهَا وَبَرْدُهَا مِنْ جَهَنَّمَ\nUKHRUJEE YAA UMMA MILDAMIN YAA AAKILATAL LAHMI WA SHAARIBATAD DAMI HARRUHAA WA BARDUHAA MIN JAHANNAM\nGet out, O Umm Mildam, O eater of flesh and drinker of blood, whose heat and whose cold are from Hell!\nاِنْ كُنْتِ اٰمَنْتِ بِاللّٰهِ الْاَعْظَمِ اَنْ لَّا تَاْكُلِىْ لِفُلَانِ بْنِ فُلَانٍ لَحْمًا وَّلَا تَمُصِّىْ لَهٗ دَمًا\nIN KUNTI AAMANTI BILLAAHIL A'ZAMI AL LAA TA'KULEE LIFULAANIBNI FULAANIN LAHMAN WA LAA TAMUSSEE LAHOO DAMAA\nIf you believe in Allah, the Most Great, then do not eat the flesh of so-and-so, the son of so-and-so, nor suck his blood,\nوَّلَا تَنْهَكِىْ لَهٗ عَظْمًا وَّلَا تُثَوِّرِىْ عَلَيْهِ غَمًّا وَّلَا تُهَيِّجِىْ عَلَيْهِ صُدَاعًا\nWA LAA TANHAKEE LAHOO A'ZMAN WA LAA TUTHAWWIREE A'LAYHI GHAMMAN WA LAA TUHAYYIJEE A'LAYHI SUDAA'AA\nnor wear out his bones, nor stir up distress against him, nor provoke headache in him;\nوَانْتَقِلِىْ عَنْ شَعْرِهٖ وَبَشَرِهٖ وَلَحْمِهٖ وَدَمِهٖ اِلٰى مَنْ زَعَمَ اَنَّ مَعَ اللّٰهِ اِلٰهًا اٰخَرَ\nWANTAQILEE A'N SHA'RIHEE WA BASHARIHEE WA LAHMIHEE WA DAMIHEE ILAA MAN ZA'AMA ANNA MA'ALLAAHI ILAAHAN AAKHAR\nand move away from his hair, his skin, his flesh and his blood to him who claims that there is another god with Allah.\nلَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ سُبْحَانَهٗ وَتَعَالٰى عَمَّا يُشْرِكُوْنَ\nLAA ILAAHA ILLAA HUWA SUBHAANAHOO WA TA'AALAA A'MMAA YUSHRIKOON\nThere is no god but He; glory be to Him, and exalted is He above what they associate with Him.\nIn place of “so-and-so, the son of so-and-so”, mention the name of the feverish person and his father's name. Then, it is recommended to write down the name of a disbeliever or an enemy of Almighty Allah.\n(7) It is advised to tie on the right arm of the feverish person a sheet of paper (or the like) on which the following inscription has been written, beginning with [Surah al-Fatihah](A5):\nبِسْمِ اللّٰهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ اَلْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ رَبِّ الْعَالَمِيْنَ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ مَالِكِ يَوْمِ الدِّيْنِ\nBISMILLAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEMIL HAMDU LILLAAHI RABBIL A'ALAMEENAR RAHMAANIR RAHEEMI MAALIKI YAWMID DEEN\nIn the Name of Allah, the Beneficent, the Merciful. All praise is due to Allah, the Lord of the worlds, the Beneficent, the Merciful, Master of the Day of Judgment.\nاِيَّاكَ نَعْبُدُ وَاِيَّاكَ نَسْتَعِيْنُ اِهْدِنَا الصِّرَاطَ الْمُسْتَقِيْمَ صِرَاطَ الَّذِيْنَ اَنْعَمْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ غَيْرِ الْمَغْضُوْبِ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلَا الضَّاۤلِّيْنَ\nIYYAAKA NA'BUDU WA IYYAAKA NASTA'EENU IHDINAS SIRAATAL MUSTAQEEMA SIRAATAL LADHEENA AN'AMTA A'LAYHIM GHAYRIL MAGHDOOBI A'LAYHIM WA LAD DAALLEEN\nYou do we serve and You do we beseech for help. Keep us on the right path, the path of those upon whom You have bestowed favors, not (the path) of those upon whom Your wrath is brought down, nor of those who go astray.\nبِسْمِ اللّٰهِ وَبِاللّٰهِ اَعُوْذُ بِكَلِمَاتِ اللّٰهِ التَّاۤمَّاتِ كُلِّهَا الَّتِىْ لَا يُجَاوِزُهُنَّ بَرٌّ وَّلَا فَاجِرٌ\nBISMILLAAHI WA BILLAAHI A'OODHU BIKALIMAATILLAAHIT TAAMMAATI KULLIHAL LATEE LAA YUJAAWIZUHUNNA BARRUN WA LAA FAAJIR\nIn the Name of Allah and by Allah, I seek refuge in all the perfect words of Allah, which neither the righteous nor the wicked can overstep,\nمِنْ شَرِّ مَا خَلَقَ وَذَرَءَ وَبَرَءَ وَمِنْ شَرِّ الْهَاۤمَّةِ وَالسَّاۤمَّةِ وَالْعَاۤمَّةِ وَاللَّاۤمَّةِ\nMIN SHARRI MAA KHALAQA WA DHARA'A WA BARA'A WA MIN SHARRIL HAAMMATI WAS SAAMMATI WAL A'AMMATI WAL LAAMMAH\nfrom the evil of what He has created, multiplied and brought into being, and from the evil of every venomous creature, every poisonous one, every common affliction and every evil eye,\nوَمِنْ شَرِّ طَوَارِقِ اللَّيْلِ وَالنَّهَارِ وَمِنْ شَرِّ فُسَّاقِ الْعَرَبِ وَالْعَجَمِ\nWA MIN SHARRI TAWAARIQIL LAYLI WAN NAHAARI WA MIN SHARRI FUSSAAQIL A'RABI WAL A'JAM\nfrom the evil of what comes by night and by day, from the evil of the wicked among the Arabs and the non-Arabs,\nوَمِنْ شَرِّ فَسَقَةِ الْجِنِّ وَالْاِنْسِ وَمِنْ شَرِّ الشَّيْطَانِ وَشَرَكِهٖ وَمِنْ شَرِّ كُلِّ ذِىْ شَرٍّ\nWA MIN SHARRI FASAQATIL JINNI WAL INSI WA MIN SHARRISH SHAYTAANI WA SHARAKIHEE WA MIN SHARRI KULLI DHEE SHARR\nfrom the evil of the wicked among jinn and men, from the evil of Satan and his snares, and from the evil of every evil being,\nوَّمِنْ شَرِّ كُلِّ دَاۤبَّةٍ هُوَ اٰخِذٌ بِنَاصِيَتِهَا اِنَّ رَبِّىْ عَلٰى صِرَاطٍ مُّسْتَقِيْمٍ\nWA MIN SHARRI KULLI DAABBATIN HUWA AAKHIDHUN BINAASIYATIHAA INNA RABBEE A'LAA SIRAATIM MUSTAQEEM\nand from the evil of every creature that moves, whose forelock He holds; surely my Lord is on the right path.\nرَبَّنَا عَلَيْكَ تَوَكَّلْنَا وَاِلَيْكَ اَنَبْنَا وَاِلَيْكَ الْمَصِيْرُ\nRABBANAA A'LAYKA TAWAKKALNAA WA ILAYKA ANABNAA WA ILAYKAL MASEER\nOur Lord! On You do we rely, to You do we turn, and to You is the eventual coming. (60:4)\nيَا نَارُ كُوْنِىْ بَرْدًا وَّسَلَامًا عَلٰى اِبْرَاهِيْمَ وَاَرَادُوْا بِهٖ كَيْدًا فَجَعَلْنَاهُمُ الْاَخْسَرِيْنَ\nYAA NAARU KOONEE BARDAN WA SALAAMAN A'LAA IBRAAHEEMA WA ARAADOO BIHEE KAYDAN FAJA'ALNAAHUMUL AKHSAREEN\nO fire! be coolness and peace upon Ibrahim. And they intended a plan against him, but We made them the greater losers. (21:69-70)\nبَرْدًا وَّسَلَامًا عَلٰى فُلَانِ بْنِ فُلَانَةَ\nBARDAN WA SALAAMAN A'LAA FULAANIBNI FULAANAH\nCoolness and peace upon so-and-so, the son of so-and-so.\nرَبَّنَا لَا تُؤَاخِذْنَا اِنْ نَّسِيْنَا اَوْ اَخْطَاْنَا رَبَّنَا وَلَا تَحْمِلْ عَلَيْنَا اِصْرًا كَمَا حَمَلْتَهٗ عَلَى الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِنَا\nRABBANAA LAA TU'AAKHIDHNAA IN NASEENAA AW AKHTA'NAA RABBANAA WA LAA TAHMIL A'LAYNAA ISRAN KAMAA HAMALTAHOO A'LAL LADHEENA MIN QABLINAA\nOur Lord! do not punish us if we forget or make a mistake. Our Lord! do not lay on us a burden as You laid on those before us.\nرَبَّنَا وَلَا تُحَمِّلْنَا مَا لَا طَاقَةَ لَنَا بِهٖ وَاعْفُ عَنَّا وَاغْفِرْ لَنَا وَارْحَمْنَا اَنْتَ مَوْلَانَا فَانْصُرْنَا عَلَى الْقَوْمِ الْكَافِرِيْنَ\nRABBANAA WA LAA TUHAMMILNAA MAA LAA TAAQATA LANAA BIHEE WA'FU A'NNAA WAGHFIR LANAA WARHAMNAA ANTA MAWLAANAA FANSURNAA A'LAL QAWMIL KAAFIREEN\nOur Lord! do not impose upon us that which we have not the strength to bear; pardon us, grant us protection and have mercy on us; You are our Patron, so help us against the unbelieving people. (2:286)\nحَسْبِىَ اللّٰهُ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ فَاتَّخِذْهُ وَكِيْلًا وَّتَوَكَّلْ عَلَى الْحَىِّ الَّذِىْ لَا يَمُوْتُ\nHASBIYALLAAHU LAA ILAAHA ILLAA HUWA FATTAKHIDH-HU WAKEELAN WA TAWAKKAL A'LAL HAYYIL LADHEE LAA YAMOOT\nAllah is sufficient for me; there is no god but He; so take Him for a protector, and rely on the Ever-living Who dies not,\nوَسَبِّحْ بِحَمْدِهٖ وَكَفٰى بِهٖ بِذُنُوْبِ عِبَادِهٖ خَبِيْرًا بَصِيْرًا\nWA SABBIH BIHAMDIHEE WA KAFAA BIHEE BIDHUNOOBI I'BAADIHEE KHABEERAN BASEERAA\nand celebrate His praise; and Sufficient is He as being aware of the faults of His servants, All-seeing.\nلَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ وَحْدَهٗ لَا شَرِيْكَ لَهٗ صَدَقَ وَعْدَهٗ وَنَصَرَ عَبْدَهٗ وَهَزَمَ الْاَحْزَابَ وَحْدَهٗ\nLAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAHU WAHDAHOO LAA SHAREEKA LAHOO SADAQA WA'DAHOO WA NASARA A'BDAHOO WA HAZAMAL AHZAABA WAHDAH\nThere is no god but Allah, One, having no partner. He fulfilled His promise, gave victory to His servant, and alone defeated the confederates.\nمَا شَاۤءَ اللّٰهُ لَا قُوَّةَ اِلَّا بِاللّٰهِ كَتَبَ اللّٰهُ لَاَغْلِبَنَّ اَنَا وَرُسُلِىْ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ قَوِىٌّ عَزِيْزٌ\nMAA SHAA'ALLAAHU LAA QUWWATA ILLAA BILLAAHI KATABALLAAHU LA-AGHLIBANNA ANAA WA RUSULEE INNALLAAHA QAWIYYUN A'ZEEZ\nIt is as Allah has pleased; there is no power save in Allah. Allah has written down: I and My messengers will most certainly prevail; surely Allah is Strong, Mighty. (58:21)\nاِنَّ حِزْبَ اللّٰهِ هُمُ الْغَالِبُوْنَ وَمَنْ يَّعْتَصِمْ بِاللّٰهِ فَقَدْ هُدِىَ اِلٰى صِرَاطٍ مُّسْتَقِيْمٍ\nINNA HIZBALLAAHI HUMUL GHAALIBOONA WA MAN YA'TASIM BILLAAHI FAQAD HUDIYA ILAA SIRAATIM MUSTAQEEM\nSurely the party of Allah are they that shall be triumphant; and whoever holds fast to Allah, he indeed is guided to the right path.\nوَصَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَّاٰلِهِ الطَّيِّبِيْنَ الطَّاهِرِيْنَ\nWA SALLALLAAHU A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALIHIT TAYYIBEENAT TAAHIREEN\nAnd may Allah bless Muhammad and his Household, the good, the pure.\nIn place of “so-and-so, the son of so-and-so”, mention the name of the feverish person and his mother's name.\n(8) On three pieces of sugar, the following three phrases may be written, and the feverish person may eat them on the mornings of three days as the first thing he eats, one piece each day. On the first piece:\nعَقَدْتُ بِاِذْنِ اللّٰهِ\nA'QADTU BI-IDHNILLAAH\nI have bound it, by the permission of Allah.\nOn the second piece:\nشَدَدْتُ بِاِذْنِ اللّٰهِ\nSHADADTU BI-IDHNILLAAH\nI have made it fast, by the permission of Allah.\nOn the third piece:\nسَكَنْتُ بِاِذْنِ اللّٰهِ\nSAKANTU BI-IDHNILLAAH\nI have stilled it, by the permission of Allah.\nA Supplicatory Prayer against Tenesmus\nIt is reported that a man complained to Imam Musa al-Kazim (a.s.) of continuous tenesmus (a frequent, painful urge to defecate). As treatment, the Imam (a.s.) taught the man to say the following supplicatory prayer after the Night Prayer:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ مَا كَانَ مِنْ خَيْرٍ فَمِنْكَ لَا حَمْدَ لِىْ فِيْهِ\nALLAAHUMMA MAA KAANA MIN KHAYRIN FAMINKA LAA HAMDA LEE FEEH\nO Allah, whatever good there is, it is from You, and I deserve no praise for it;\nوَمَا عَمِلْتُ مِنْ سُوْۤءٍ فَقَدْ حَذَّرْتَنِيْهِ لَا عُذْرَ لِىْ فِيْهِ\nWA MAA A'MILTU MIN SOO'IN FAQAD HADHDHARTANEEHI LAA U'DHRA LEE FEEH\nand whatever evil I have done, You had warned me against it, and I have no excuse for it.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّىْۤ اَعُوْذُ بِكَ اَنْ اَتَّكِلَ عَلٰى مَا لَا حَمْدَ لِىْ فِيْهِ اَوْ اٰمَنَ مِمَّا لَا عُذْرَ لِىْ فِيْهِ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE A'OODHU BIKA AN ATTAKILA A'LAA MAA LAA HAMDA LEE FEEHI AW AAMANA MIMMAA LAA U'DHRA LEE FEEH\nO Allah, I seek refuge in You from relying on that for which I deserve no praise, or feeling secure in that for which I have no excuse.\nA Supplicatory Prayer against Stomach Gurgling\nImam Musa al-Kazim (a.s.) is also reported to have advised the same supplicatory prayer, said after the Night Prayer, for those who suffer from stomach gurgling. A man had said to him, “I suffer from stomach gurgling that never stops, and I feel embarrassed when the people I speak to hear it. So please pray to Allah to cure me of it.”\nImam al-Sadiq (a.s.), advising those who suffer from stomach gurgling, said, “Black cumin may be mixed with honey and then eaten.”\nA Supplicatory Prayer against Leprosy\nYunus reported that whitish patches appeared between his eyes. He complained of this disease to Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.), who directed him to a treatment, saying: Perform the ritual bathing (ghusl), offer a two-unit prayer, and say this supplicatory prayer:\nيَاۤ اَللّٰهُ يَا رَحْمٰنُ يَا رَحِيْمُ يَا سَمِيْعَ الدَّعَوَاتِ يَا مُعْطِىَ الْخَيْرَاتِ\nYAA ALLAAHU YAA RAHMAANU YAA RAHEEMU YAA SAMEE'AD DA'AWAATI YAA MU'TIYAL KHAYRAAT\nO Allah, O Beneficent, O Merciful, O Hearer of supplications, O Giver of good things,\nاَعْطِنِىْ خَيْرَ الدُّنْيَا وَخَيْرَ الْاٰخِرَةِ وَقِنِىْ شَرَّ الدُّنْيَا وَشَرَّ الْاٰخِرَةِ\nA'TINEE KHAYRAD DUNYAA WA KHAYRAL AAKHIRATI WA QINEE SHARRAD DUNYAA WA SHARRAL AAKHIRAH\ngive me the good of this world and the good of the Hereafter, and protect me from the evil of this world and the evil of the Hereafter,\nوَاَذْهِبْ عَنِّىْ مَا اَجِدُ فَقَدْ غَاظَنِى الْاَمْرُ وَاَحْزَنَنِىْ\nWA ADH-HIB A'NNEE MAA AJIDU FAQAD GHAAZANIL AMRU WA AHZANANEE\nand remove from me what I suffer, for the matter has angered and grieved me.\nReporting the same narration, the author of 'Uddat al-Da'i reports Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) as saying: At the beginning of the last third of the night, perform the ritual ablution and offer the prayer you usually offer at this time. In the second prostration of the first two units of the prayer, say the following while you are prostrating:\nيَا عَلِىُّ يَا عَظِيْمُ يَا رَحْمٰنُ يَا رَحِيْمُ يَا سَامِعَ الدَّعَوَاتِ يَا مُعْطِىَ الْخَيْرَاتِ\nYAA A'LIYYU YAA A'ZEEMU YAA RAHMAANU YAA RAHEEMU YAA SAAMI'AD DA'AWAATI YAA MU'TIYAL KHAYRAAT\nO Most High, O Great, O Beneficent, O Merciful, O Hearer of supplications, O Giver of good things,\nصَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَّاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ وَّاَعْطِنِىْ مِنْ خَيْرِ الدُّنْيَا وَالْاٰخِرَةِ مَاۤ اَنْتَ اَهْلُهٗ\nSALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMADIN WA A'TINEE MIN KHAYRID DUNYAA WAL AAKHIRATI MAA ANTA AHLUH\nbless Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad, and give me of the good of this world and the Hereafter that which befits You,\nوَاصْرِفْ عَنِّىْ مِنْ شَرِّ الدُّنْيَا وَالْاٰخِرَةِ مَاۤ اَنْتَ اَهْلُهٗ\nWASRIF A'NNEE MIN SHARRID DUNYAA WAL AAKHIRATI MAA ANTA AHLUH\nand turn away from me of the evil of this world and the Hereafter that which befits You,\nوَاَذْهِبْ عَنِّىْ هٰذَا الْوَجَعَ فَاِنَّهٗ قَدْ غَاظَنِىْ وَاَحْزَنَنِىْ\nWA ADH-HIB A'NNEE HAADHAL WAJA'A FA-INNAHOO QAD GHAAZANEE WA AHZANANEE\nand remove from me this pain, for it has angered and grieved me.\nYou may pray to Almighty Allah with insistence.\nYunus added, “Before I returned to Kufah, Almighty Allah had removed from me all traces of that disease.”\nFor this disease, as well as for hemorrhoids, it is reported that one may write [Surah Ya-Sin](A40) with honey in a cup, then wash the cup and drink the water.\nIt is also reported that the soil of Imam al-Husayn's tomb, kneaded with rainwater, may be taken for it."
